  "notes": "The author of this lane's guitar-trap grammar, and the research names his construction unit exactly: \"a four-note melody over a minor riff\". That is not a paraphrase to be softened — `motifPitchCount` is a flat 4 and the families are the two the paragraph writes out, i–VI–III–VII and i–VII–VI, over 4 bars with no modulation. The second exact claim is the drums: \"triple-time (32nd/triplet) hi-hats as the Southern-rap signifier against the rock instrumentation; fills are hat rolls, **never kit fills**\". So `hihat.fill` fires at 0.8 in 32nds and triplets, `rolls.freqPerBar` sits at the top of this batch's band at 0.60, and `percs.lanes` is empty — there is no kit to fill with. The snare-roll block is the batch fingerprint rather than a reading of the record, and it is deliberately the quietest use of it here. Third, the sole melodic instrument is electric guitar treated with \"reverberation and low-pass filters\" for a cinematic haze: `timbreHint` `clean_guitar` in a guitar register of 52–76, `articulation` `legato`, and the 808 doubling that root one to two octaves down at `followRootsProb` 0.96 with `glideProb` 0.1 (\"minimal glide\"). \"Vocal doubles and moaned backing vocals as countermelody\" is `octave_echo` weighted over `answer_lick` at a +12 offset. ⚠ `medium` because the research rates it high-medium; his role, collaborators and the harmonic/effects grammar are directly documented, and the one INFERRED parameter is the tempo, which the paragraph derives from \"mid-tempo\" plus catalogue.",
